course: dictionary
lesson: 305
title: Analyse: look closely, part by part
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To analyse something means to look at it closely and carefully, part by part, so you understand how it works. Quick looking is not enough. «Sports teams already use AI to analyse games and players' movements» means they study each move, not just watch the game go by.
explain: Context clues help. In «analyse the data» or «analyse the results», the word tells you to think hard. At school you might analyse a poem: look at its words and how they work, then explain what it means. Analyse is a verb, so it changes: analyses, analysed, analysing.
explain: «Too much analysing can take the fun out of a game.» Analysing is the -ing form of the same verb. The sentence shows that careful study is not always the best way to enjoy something. In the USA the spelling is analyze, but the meaning is the same.
fact: Analyse means to look at something closely, part by part, to understand it.
fact: In science and maths, to analyse means to study data, results or a sample to find patterns or what it is made of.
fact: At school, to analyse a poem or story means to explain how it works and what it means.
fact: Analyse is a verb: analyses, analysed, analysing.
fact: The US spelling is analyze. «The Ethics Bowl» is a similar competition in the USA, where teams analyse cases and respond to each other.
exercise: «Sports teams already use AI to analyse games.» What does analyse mean here? | *Look closely at something, part by part, to understand it | Forget about it | Watch quickly without thinking | Buy something new
exercise: In maths, what do you do when you analyse a graph? | Colour it in only | Draw a picture of a cat | *Read it and explain the patterns | Throw it away
exercise: Which sentence shows someone analysing carefully? | They read it with their eyes shut | They put the poem in a bag | *They read the poem line by line and explained what each image shows | They glanced at the poem and said "nice"
test: Mia has to analyse a poem for school. What should she do? | Skip the poem | Copy the title only | Read it once quickly and guess | *Look at its words and how they work, then explain what it means
test: Which form fits this sentence? "Yesterday, she ___ the results." | analysing | *analysed | analyses | analyse
exam: Jayden says analyse and analyze mean different things. Is he right? | No, analyze is a noun for a bag | Yes, analyze means to sleep | *No, they mean the same; analyze is the US spelling | Yes, analyze means to forget something
